  "owner_map_request": {
    "text": "Ah, BTW add minimap/world map to S2",
    "sha256": "cc35b8fb3086542077355096c9852e7c98ff764afe44b689d6849f4d19031ebd"
  },
  "owner_ui_request": {
    "text": "And let's improve UI. Design a UI prototype (4 main screens - world loading before connecting to the server, world generation, game screen, world map). Try to improve visual quality, UX, enjoyment.\n\nFor the game, add to HUD:\n\n1. Loaded chunks\n2. Memory usage\n3. Current climate in local place (temperature, humidity, salinity if any, etc)\n\nMinimap will display some local area (e.g. at L1/L2) + orientation (N/E/S/W)",
    "sha256": "1ee781e9edaafb4f479014e1ac5aae7b4eed9db52d9b9dc1e4f88043f3df46c7"
  },
  "owner_ui_capability_correction": {
    "text": "This UI look not like something achievable in the current snapshot... Like, we now only have text rendering. Plus we can render some background for the loading screen, we can render the map. But not much more. We don't have, e.g., buttons.",
    "sha256": "a4abd0ab22cfa836c86fb3a7ead4121939f71dae419148ab76f23352602efcf7"
  },
  "owner_ui_refinement": {
    "text": "Not bad. But several moments:\n\n1. World loading initial screen probably needs some simple rendering of the game as it's background\n2. During world generation, the process of world creation must probably be depicted in more detail and be more visually attractive (even if it actually differs somewhat from it's actually generated)\n3. Do not diplay things like salinity where it's not applicable\n4. Redesign the in-game block so it distracts the player less and is also more visually appealing",
    "sha256": "c0e489e66e211b1fb7def52fadc359ede570daff7590144e4328ac6641debf33"
  },
  "owner_loading_background": {
    "text": "Maybe for the background you can use a pre-rendered screen from the game (without HUD)",
    "sha256": "5c21cbd5e83940261122cc73eb28a16cbe39d604f08784e040258782e39f934a"
  },
  "prototype_assets": "../prototypes/s2-ui/assets/provenance.json",
  "rejected_concepts": "The initial image-generated illustrated concepts exceeded the owner-retained UI primitives and are excluded from this design.",
  "owner_ui_preservation_feedback": {
    "text": "1. Screen very poor. Not even the globe is visible. Use at least one from the ongoing S1 dev. Or well, leave it as is in the prototype - when we'll begin S2 implementation, naturally we'll have some screens from S1 already\n2. World generation stiil bad. It lacks dynamics, it lacks visual attraction\n3. Minimap looks a bit dull and as if it's color palette differs from that of the other game too much. N/E/S/W also look too inconspicuous.\n4. Now the in-game hood lacks details. Where are FPS, XYZ, etc? I asked to add new information, not to remove the existing one",
    "sha256": "d9911c273f50cd258612f3d6e1b2feb14d0fe04bd1b9b070e86dc8960d65e68c"
  },
  "owner_ui_principles": {
    "text": "Like, the UI must be: 1. authentic and using what we can use now, 2. visually captivating, 3. useful/informative/convenient, 4. easy to understand and use\nYou can change some pieces of design or come up with new ideas yourself",
    "sha256": "728c86af0e3ea9da04743c2cf80f4d151291793b10bcb9d4122eaf19c597b9ae"
  },
  "additional_hud_sources": {
    "src/client/render/DebugHud.cpp": "81cee870ca0d8d26f8393ba6044134ec017c84bffad79adbe01019d28ee2b756",
    "src/client/include/client/render/DebugHud.hpp": "a2c20165783d0c8db43357b389c9c4b84118658e44382e4f9f35e4e26353e918",
